<% content_for :title, "Button" %>
<div class="mb-8">
  <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Forms</p>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">Button</h1>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground">
    The submit button of a Rails form, the trigger for a <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">data-turbo-confirm</code> or a
    <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">data-turbo-stream</code> link, and the link that has to look like an action. It carries whatever
    Turbo attribute you forward to it, shows a submitting state through <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">data-turbo-disable-with</code>,
    and renders a real <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">&lt;button&gt;</code> — or an <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">&lt;a&gt;</code> when you pass
    <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">href:</code>. Six variants across four sizes, drawn entirely from the design tokens.
  </p>
</div>

<%# Preview %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Preview</h2>
<div id="button-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3 p-12 mb-8">
  <% %i[default secondary outline ghost link destructive].each do |variant| %>
    <%= render(Ui::ButtonComponent.new(variant: variant)) { variant.to_s.capitalize } %>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%# Variants %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Variants</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg border border-border divide-y divide-border mb-8">
  <% [
    [:default,     "The primary action. One per view, ideally."],
    [:secondary,   "A supporting action of equal weight to the page, less weight than default."],
    [:outline,     "A bordered action that sits quietly on any surface."],
    [:ghost,       "Toolbar and icon actions — no chrome until hover."],
    [:link,        "Reads as text; use when the action is navigation."],
    [:destructive, "Irreversible actions. Pair it with a confirm."],
  ].each do |variant, description| %>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-6 px-5 py-4">
      <div class="w-36 shrink-0"><%= render(Ui::ButtonComponent.new(variant: variant)) { variant.to_s.capitalize } %></div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-primary mb-0.5">variant: :<%= variant %></p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground"><%= description %></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%# Sizes %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Sizes</h2>
<div id="button-sizes-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 p-8 mb-8">
  <%= render(Ui::ButtonComponent.new(size: :sm)) { "Small" } %>
  <%= render(Ui::ButtonComponent.new) { "Default" } %>
  <%= render(Ui::ButtonComponent.new(size: :lg)) { "Large" } %>
  <%= render Ui::ButtonComponent.new(size: :icon, variant: :outline, aria: { label: "Add item" }) do %>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/>
    </svg>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%# Full matrix %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Variant × size</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-muted">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Variant</th>
        <% %i[sm default lg icon].each do |size| %>
          <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider"><%= size %></th>
        <% end %>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
      <% %i[default secondary outline ghost link destructive].each do |variant| %>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary"><%= variant %></td>
          <% %i[sm default lg].each do |size| %>
            <td class="px-4 py-3"><%= render(Ui::ButtonComponent.new(variant: variant, size: size)) { "Button" } %></td>
          <% end %>
          <td class="px-4 py-3">
            <%= render Ui::ButtonComponent.new(variant: variant, size: :icon, aria: { label: "Add" }) do %>
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/>
              </svg>
            <% end %>
          </td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<%# States %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">States</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 p-8 mb-4">
  <%= render(Ui::ButtonComponent.new) { "Enabled" } %>
  <%= render(Ui::ButtonComponent.new(disabled: true)) { "Disabled" } %>
  <%= render(Ui::ButtonComponent.new(href: "#", variant: :outline)) { "Link" } %>
  <%= render(Ui::ButtonComponent.new(href: "#", variant: :outline, disabled: true)) { "Disabled link" } %>
  <%= render Ui::ButtonComponent.new(variant: :secondary) do %>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/>
    </svg>
    Icon + label
  <% end %>
</div>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-8">
  Tab to a button to see the focus ring — it is drawn from the <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">--ring</code> token,
  so it follows the theme. A disabled <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">href</code> button
  drops its href and reports <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-disabled</code>, so it is inert without JavaScript.
</p>

<%# Submitting %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Submitting</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  Give a submit button <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">data: { turbo_disable_with: "Saving…" }</code> and, while the form submits, it is disabled,
  keeps its size, shows the text — with a spinner or a pulse if you ask — and announces it to screen readers. The
  <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">ui--turbo-disable-with</code> controller in your layout does this for every form; see
  <%= link_to "Turbo Disable With", turbo_disable_with_path, class: "text-primary underline" %>. This one waits a second and a half
  for its response.
</p>
<div id="button-submitting-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 p-8 mb-8">
  <%= form_with url: demo_submit_path do %>
    <%= render(Ui::ButtonComponent.new(type: "submit", data: { turbo_disable_with: "Saving…", turbo_disable_style: "spinner" })) { "Save changes" } %>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%# Usage %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Usage</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-border mb-8">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-muted px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">ERB</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#button-usage" class="text-xs text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-card px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed" tabindex="0"><code id="button-usage" class="text-card-foreground"><%= h(example_button_usage) %></code></pre>
</div>

<%# Options %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Options</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-muted">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Name</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Type</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Default</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
      <% [
        ["variant", "Symbol", ":default",  "One of :default, :destructive, :outline, :secondary, :ghost, :link."],
        ["size",    "Symbol", ":default",  "One of :default, :sm, :lg, :icon. The first three are the control scale Input, Select and Textarea share, so controls at one size line up; :icon is a square at the default height."],
        ["href",    "String", "nil",       "When present the component renders an <a> instead of a <button>."],
        ["type",    "String", '"button"',  "Button type. Ignored on the <a> form."],
        ["class",   "String", "nil",       "Merged over the variant classes with tailwind_merge — the caller always wins."],
        ["…",       "Any",    "—",         "Every other keyword (id:, name:, disabled:, data:, aria:, …) is forwarded to the root element."],
      ].each do |name, type, default, desc| %>
        <tr class="hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary"><%= name %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= type %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground"><%= default %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= desc %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<%# Overriding classes %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Overriding classes</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  Your <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">class:</code> replaces a conflicting default,
  but only a default with the same modifier. Some defaults carry one: a button with an icon uses
  <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">has-[&gt;svg]:px-3</code>, which still applies over a plain
  <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">px-2</code>. To override it, pass the same modifier:
</p>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-border mb-8">
  <pre class="bg-card px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed" tabindex="0"><code class="text-card-foreground">&lt;%= render Ui::ButtonComponent.new(class: "px-2 has-[&gt;svg]:px-2") do %&gt;…&lt;% end %&gt;</code></pre>
</div>

<%# Accessibility %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Accessibility</h2>
<ul class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-2 mb-8 list-disc ps-5">
  <li>A real <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">&lt;button&gt;</code>, <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">type="button"</code> unless you say <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">type: "submit"</code>,
      so a button inside a form never submits it by accident.</li>
  <li>A disabled <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">href</code> button drops its href and reports <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">role="link" aria-disabled="true"</code>,
      so it is inert and announced as unavailable, with or without JavaScript.</li>
  <li>An icon-only button has no text to be named by: give it <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria: { label: }</code>. The
      <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">&lt;svg&gt;</code> itself should be <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-hidden</code>.</li>
  <li>The focus ring is an outline drawn from <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">--ring</code>, so it follows the theme and stays visible in
      forced-colors mode.</li>
</ul>

<%# Not this %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">When not to use it</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-8">
  Navigation that reads as text is a plain link, not <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">variant: :link</code>. An on/off setting that stays
  pressed is a toggle or a switch, which the kit doesn't ship. And a destructive action on its own is one click from
  data loss: put a <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">data-turbo-confirm</code> on it, which the
  <%= link_to "Confirm Dialog", confirm_dialog_path, class: "text-primary underline" %> answers.
</p>
